<title>JAPAN: Japan July crude oil imports fall 16.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July crude oil imports fall 16.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) on Monday issued the following data on crude oil imports during July 1996.</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) mth/mth% yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	     901	  5,667    -42.4    -57.1</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 3,410	 21,449    - 5.6    -25.7</p>
<p> Kuwait	 1,012	  6,365    -19.6    +11.8</p>
<p> Neutral Zone 1,069	  6,724    +61.5    - 3.4</p>
<p> Qatar	  1,195	  7,517    -12.6    - 7.6</p>
<p> Oman	     932	  5,862    + 6.3    -41.5</p>
<p> UAE	    5,460	 34,343    + 3.5    + 1.1</p>
<p> Yemen	    136	    855     ----    + 0.8</p>
<p> China	  1,008	  6,340     -12.0   -12.0</p>
<p> Malaysia	 237	  1,491     +24.7   +49.6</p>
<p> Brunei	   137	    862     -55.5   -29.2</p>
<p> Indonesia    1,529	  9,617     +20.1   - 7.7</p>
<p> Vietnam	  256	  1,610     -32.1   -39.9</p>
<p> Mexico	   555	  3,491     - 0.9   +91.6</p>
<p> Australia	181	  1,138     -22.4   -50.8</p>
<p> TOTAL	 18,018	113,324     - 3.7   -16.1</p>
